WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:07.520
Hey David, is it fair not to let yang and
Tulsi speak during the debates?

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:13.049
It's not, I've, I've talked about this, we
did a big piece about this on the Monday show

00:00:13.049 --> 00:00:16.920
where I explained, I think there are too many
people on the stage.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:21.610
I think there should be five, maybe six at
this point at the most based on who still

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:27.441
has a shot and how far into this thing we
are, but if you make the stage you should

00:00:27.441 --> 00:00:29.130
get roughly equal time.

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:35.570
I don't agree with the network making editorial
decisions to say if you're pulling better

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:36.810
you will get more time.

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:41.720
If you're pulling poorly you'll get less time
except where we want to do it differently.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:46.750
And what we saw in the fifth MSNBC, the fifth
debate which was on MSNBC last week was that

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:53.830
for example, Andrew Yang got drastically less
time than his polling support would predict.

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:55.330
On the other hand, Pete booted.

00:00:55.330 --> 00:01:02.030
Judge was the biggest beneficiary who got
significantly more time on screen talk time

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:04.159
then his polling would suggest.

00:01:04.159 --> 00:01:10.219
So I do not think it's fair for yang and Tulsi
to speak during the, I'm no fan of Tulsa's

00:01:10.219 --> 00:01:14.770
and she has no shot, but if she makes the
debate she should get the same amount of time

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:16.219
as everybody else.

00:01:16.219 --> 00:01:19.459
Andrew Yang I like, I don't think he's going
to be the nominee.

00:01:19.459 --> 00:01:21.020
I've interviewed him on the program perfectly.

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:22.020
Nice guy.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:23.020
Has good ideas.

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:26.529
He should get the same amount of time as everybody
else.

00:01:26.529 --> 00:01:31.570
If he has made the debate, if your argument
is these people don't really have a shot at

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:35.469
winning, so it makes sense not to give them
much time, well then they shouldn't be on

00:01:35.469 --> 00:01:36.469
the stage.

00:01:36.469 --> 00:01:42.549
If that's your, uh, your, the DNC is running
the election, they should have requirements

00:01:42.549 --> 00:01:45.639
for making the debate stages that make sense.

00:01:45.639 --> 00:01:50.880
They should not be leaving it up to the whims
of for-profit media who may have all sorts

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.729
of different priorities themselves.

00:01:52.729 --> 00:02:00.149
MSNBC 10 trending towards the sort of more
establishment centrist Democrats like Joe

00:02:00.149 --> 00:02:04.909
Biden, uh, Pete, Buddha, judge, they seem
to sort of have reluctantly made the call

00:02:04.909 --> 00:02:09.390
that if it is going to be a more progressive
candidate that wins between Warren and Bernie.

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:13.590
They prefer Warren's or they've been talking
up Warren over, over Bernie and they've been

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:18.950
particularly unfair to Andrew Yang referring
to him as John Yang at least once, if not

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:19.950
more.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:24.170
They put a poll up on the screen a couple
of weeks ago where they just ignored the Andrew

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:28.100
Angus wasn't on the screen even though he
was pulling, I think in that poll 3% they

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:34.850
had people on screen who were polling to just
no explanation why John Yang or as he's actually

00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:37.150
called Andrew Yang wasn't there.

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:38.590
So I want to be really clear.

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:41.060
This is not me being a yang ganger or anything.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:45.580
I've said I'm a, I'm a Bernie Warren guy,
but fair is fair.

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:50.520
And if you make the stage, you should get
the time that everybody else gets.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:52.300
It should be evenly distributed.

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:59.050
If in a poll, you're in sixth place, you shouldn't
show one through five, skip person number

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:01.920
six and then seven, eight, nine, whatever.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:03.940
You should just put the person up there.

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:04.940
That's it.

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:05.940
It's just not fair.

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:07.130
And it's bizarre and it's strange.

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:12.800
And to your question, it's not fair to let
Andrew Yang and Tulsi, uh, uh, uh, speak so

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:17.380
little when they have made the debate stage
based on the requirements that have been put

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:19.140
in place by the DNC.

